## Context

PR #203 (ticket 0178) extended the unknown-flag rejection convention to
check, close, log, label/unlabel, init. A celebrate sweep found five
remaining commands with the same class of defect:

- `archive.go` cmdArchive: the arg loop has `else if !strings.HasPrefix(a, "-")`
  which silently *drops* unknown `-`-prefixed args rather than erroring.
- `migrate.go` cmdMigrate: raw `args[0]` with no flag-loop guard.
- `nextid.go` cmdNextID: raw `args[0]` with no flag-loop guard.
- `validate.go` cmdValidate: unknown `--flag` falls through to `os.Stat("--flag")`
  and emits "WARNING: skipping" instead of a hard error.
- `list.go` cmdList: unknown `--xyz` tokens fall through to the label-filter
  accumulator, silently treated as label names instead of erroring.

## Relevant files

- `src/go/archive.go`, `migrate.go`, `nextid.go`, `validate.go`, `list.go`
- `src/go/rm.go` — reference implementation of the convention

## Exit criteria

- [ ] All 5 commands reject unknown `-`-prefixed flags with non-zero exit
      and a "unknown flag" usage message
- [ ] Existing positional behavior unchanged — `make check` passes
- [ ] Shell integration tests cover unknown-flag rejection for each command
